---
import ItemPage from '../../layouts/ItemPage.astro';
import { CAKE_SIZES } from '../../data/cakes';

const faqs = [
  { q: 'How much is an 8-inch Dairy Queen cake?', a: 'A classic 8-inch DQ cake typically costs about $22.99. Prices vary by location, and Blizzard flavors cost more.' },
  { q: 'How many people does an 8-inch DQ cake serve?', a: 'About 8 to 10 people.' },
  { q: 'Can I buy an 8-inch DQ cake the same day?', a: 'Often, yes. Many stores keep 8-inch cakes in the freezer case and can add a short message while you wait. Custom designs need 24 to 48 hours.' },
  { q: 'What flavors does the 8-inch DQ cake come in?', a: 'The classic is chocolate and vanilla soft serve with a fudge and cookie crunch center. Some stores also offer Blizzard flavors in this size; ask your store.' },
];
---
<ItemPage
  title="Dairy Queen 8-Inch Cake: Price & Servings (2026)"
  description="An 8-inch Dairy Queen cake costs about $22.99 and serves 8–10. What is in it, same-day pickup, custom messages and how it compares to other sizes."
  name="Dairy Queen 8-Inch Round Cake"
  category={{ name: 'DQ Cakes', href: '/categories/dq-cakes' }}
  image="/Images/dq-cake-round-8inch.webp"
  imageAlt="Dairy Queen 8-inch round ice cream cake"
  badges={['Serves 8–10', 'Lowest-priced DQ cake']}
  quick="An 8-inch Dairy Queen cake costs about $22.99 and serves 8 to 10 people, making it the lowest-priced DQ cake. Many stores have them ready in the freezer, and staff can add a short message. Prices vary by location."
  from="From $22.99"
  intro="The 8-inch round is the classic small-party DQ cake: chocolate soft serve, the fudge and cookie crunch center, and vanilla soft serve with whipped icing on top. It is the easiest DQ cake to buy on short notice."
  spec={[
    ['Price', '$22.99+'],
    ['Serves', '8–10 people'],
    ['Layers', 'Chocolate and vanilla soft serve, fudge and cookie crunch center, whipped icing'],
    ['Custom options', 'Message and colors'],
    ['Lead time', 'Often same day; 24–48 hours for custom'],
  ]}
  allergens="Milk, Wheat, Soy"
  table={{ title: 'Compare DQ cake sizes and prices', ...CAKE_SIZES }}
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <h2>Who the 8-inch cake is for</h2>
  <p>It suits a family birthday or a small get-together of up to about 10 people. If more people are coming, the <a href="/items/dq-cake-round-10inch">10-inch cake</a> serves 12 to 16 for about $10 more, which works out cheaper per slice.</p>

  <h2>Buying one today</h2>
  <p>Ready-made 8-inch cakes are the ones you are most likely to find in the freezer case, so this is the best size for last-minute birthdays. Ask for a name or short message; most stores add it for free. If you want a Blizzard flavor or a special design, call 24 to 48 hours ahead.</p>

  <h2>Serving tips</h2>
  <p>Let the cake sit out for 10 to 15 minutes, then cut with a knife dipped in hot water and wiped dry. More tips are in our <a href="/blog/dq-cakes-complete-guide">DQ cake serving guide</a>, and every size is on the <a href="/categories/dq-cakes">DQ cake prices page</a>.</p>
</ItemPage>
